    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0796" n="764" xml:id="pg764"/>

                <head>371. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary of the Department of State
                    (Brubeck) to the President’s Special Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Bundy)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d371-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-06-01">June 1,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Attached is a copy of a memorandum which Mr. Goodwin took with him to the meeting
                    between the President and Ambassador Thurston on Saturday, May 26.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d371-f2"/> I understand that the memorandum was discussed at the
                    meeting and that the President gave his general approval to it.</p>
                <p>We would appreciate receiving a memorandum confirming the President’s approval of
                    the position set forth in the memorandum or some other indication of the
                    President’s decision respecting it.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d371-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">E.S. Little</hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d371-f4"
                        /></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d371-a1.xml" xpointer="d371-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d371-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d371-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Countries Series, Haiti,
                    1/61-6/62. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d371-f2" n="2" xml:id="d371-f2-content">
                <p>The meeting took place at the White House from 11:02 to 11:20 a.m. Schlesinger
                    also attended. (Ibid., President’s Appointment Book) No other record of this
                    meeting has been found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d371-f3" n="3" xml:id="d371-f3-content">
                <p>Not found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d371-f4" n="4" xml:id="d371-f4-content">
                <p>Little signed for Brubeck above Brubeck’s typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
